.TH TARADINO 6 "2026-11-26" "2026.11.26" "Taradino"

.SH NAME
Taradino \- SDL2 port of Rise of the Triad

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taradino
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TARADINO
is a port of Apogee's 3D action title Rise of the Triad, originally released in 1994.
This port duplicates the functionality of the original game on modern operating systems, including Linux, Windows, and macOS.
Portability fixes include support for 64-bit and big-endian systems.
.PP
A single executable handles both the registered and the shareware version of the game.
The version is detected at runtime from the game data that is found:
.I darkwar.wad
is preferred,
.I huntbgin.wad
is used as a fallback.
In the shareware version, the options
.BR file ,
.B filertl
and
.B filertc
are ignored.

.SH OPTIONS
Options are given without a leading dash and are case-insensitive.
.TP
.BR aim
Give aim crosshair.
.TP
.BR fullscreen
Start in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.BR window
Start in windowed mode.
.TP
.BR resolution\  \fIwidth\fPx\fIheight\fP
Specify the screen resolution to use (next parameter is widthxheight).
Valid resolutions are 320x200 and 640x400, both with aspect ratio correction.
.TP
.BR filertl\  \fIfile\fP
Used to load Userlevels (RTL files).
.TP
.BR filertc\  \fIfile\fP
Used to load Battlelevels (RTC files).
.TP
.BR file\  \fIfile\fP
Used to load WAD files.
.TP
.BR nowait
Go to the menu, skip the intro.
.TP
.BR now
Go immediately into the game with the default difficulty on level 1.
.TP
.BR nojoys
Disable check for joystick.
.TP
.BR nomouse
Disable check for mouse.
.TP
.BR nosound
Disable sound.
.TP
.BR quiet
Get rid of all startup text except for errors.
.TP
.BR slowdeath
Slow down the death rotation.
.TP
.BR ver
Version number.
.TP
.BR mapstats
Dump Map statistics to ERROR.
.TP
.BR tilestats
Dump Tile statistics to ERROR.
.TP
.BR mono
Enable mono-monitor support.
.TP
.BR screenshots
Clean screen capture for shots.
.TP
.BR pause
Pauses startup screen information.
.TP
.BR enablevr
Enable VR helmet input devices.
.TP
.BR noecho
Turn off sound reverb.
.TP
.BR demoexit
Exit program when demo is terminated.
.TP
.BR warp\  \fIlevel\fP
Warp to specific level (next parameter is level to start on).
.TP
.BR timelimit\  \fItime\fP
Play in time limit mode (next parameter is time in seconds).
.TP
.BR maxtimelimit\  \fItime\fP
Maximum time to count down from (next parameter is time in seconds).
.TP
.BR help
Display help message.
.TP
.BR dopefish
?

.SH FILES
.TP
.IR darkwar.wad ", " huntbgin.wad
Game data of the registered and the shareware version, respectively.
They are searched for in the current directory, in the directory of the executable, in the directory set at build time, in
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/games/rott
and
.I $XDG_DATA_DIRS/games/rott
(not on Windows), and in the default installation directories of the Steam, GOG and Heroic versions of the game.
.TP
.I darkwar/\fR, \fIhuntbgin/
Subdirectories of the per-user data directory (or of the directory of the executable on Windows) which hold savegames, high scores, the configuration and screenshots of the registered and the shareware version, respectively.

